            "Specifically, we evaluate the 11B-parameter T5~\\cite{raffel2020exploring} as a direct counterpart of \\modelName{}. Due to the infilling pretraining objective of the original T5 model, it cannot continue text well. Therefore, we evaluate its ``LM-adapted'' version, which is further trained with a language modeling objective~\\cite{lester2021power}. \n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "Additionally, we evaluate GPT-3~\\cite{brown2020language}, a $175$B-parameter autoregressive LM that has shown remarkable ability in following demonstrations provided in its prompt.\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\\vskip .1cm \\noindent {\\bf Instruction-tuned models.}\n",
            "In addition to our \\modelName{} (\\S\\ref{sec:our-model}), \n",
